---
// Goal: show that you can grade saved answers against your own labels and
// move a question's cut with zero new calls, and that a high probability
// is not proof.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Terminal from '../../components/Terminal.astro';
import Code from '../../components/Code.astro';
import { START_SEE } from '../../data/catalog.mjs';
import { captioned, files } from '../../data/samples.mjs';

const [suggest, diff] = captioned('start/tune', START_SEE.tune);
const key = files('start/tune').find((f) => f.name === 'shown-key.jsonl');
const proof = 'https://github.com/botassembly/thinkthen/blob/main/specification/result.md#what-a-high-probability-does-not-mean';
---
<Base title="Tune for free" description="Grade saved answers against your own labels and move a question's cut with zero new calls.">
  <h1>Tune for free</h1>
  <p class="lede">Save one run's answers. Then grade them against your own labels and read them at any cut. No request goes out, so tuning costs nothing.</p>

  <h2 id="audit">Let audit pick the cut</h2>
  <p>A saved run asked "Is this song on the album Abbey Road?" of ten Beatles songs at the cut 0.5. The key holds the right answer for each song.</p>
  <Code code={key.text} file={key.name} caption="One right answer a song." copy={false} />
  <p><code>runs audit</code> grades the saved answers against the key. It tunes a cut on one part of the songs and checks it on the rest, over many splits, and names the cut that wins most often.</p>
  <Terminal run={suggest} caption={suggest.see} />
  <p><code>runs audit --write</code> saves that cut into the question file the run came from.</p>

  <h2 id="new-cut">Read the run at the new cut</h2>
  <p><code>runs diff</code> reads the same saved answers at two cuts and shows each answer that changed.</p>
  <Terminal run={diff} caption={diff.see} />
  <p>Ten songs make a small sample. A cut tuned on ten songs fits those ten. Grade it on records you held back before you rely on it.</p>

  <h2 id="not-proof">A high probability is not proof</h2>
  <p>The model judges only the text it was shown. A probability of 0.98 says nothing about facts the text left out. In one measurement the model approved every case at 0.98 while human reviewers refused 23% of them. The <a href={proof}>result specification</a> records it. The only test of a question is a measurement against your own labelled cases.</p>

  <p class="pagelinks"><a href="/functions/audit/">runs audit</a> · <a href="/functions/diff/">runs diff</a> · <a href="/trust/">Test it before you trust it</a></p>
</Base>
